WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.680
Film Courage: Tobey when you accepted the role of Bobby
Fischer in the movie PAWN SACRIFICE, how much

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.599
research did you do on him and watching
of his mannerisms and studying who he

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:17.340
was? Tobey Maguire, Actor/Producer: I did quite a bit I watched and
listened to anything I could get my

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:25.849
hands on and kept doing that you know
for a long time.

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:30.210
Firstly to learn about him in the
beginning as we were setting out to

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:36.480
figure out what the movie was I you know
read a bunch and watched as much as I

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.250
could find and then later as we
had we were going towards making the

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:46.289
movie then I would just I would just
listen to him constantly or you know

00:00:46.289 --> 00:00:54.660
watch interviews every day. Film Courage: Did your
feelings or opinion about him change in

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.059
any way after playing him and and being
immersed in his whole world for however

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:06.000
long the film shoot was? Tobey: You know I it's an
interesting thing when you're when

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:11.240
you're playing a character or when I'm
when I'm playing a character because I'm

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:18.509
basically going through a process where
I'm not looking to be reductive at all

00:01:18.509 --> 00:01:26.369
or to judge the person. I could I could
from a different point of view talk

00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:30.810
about Bobby and talk about some of the
things he said and say they were awful

00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:36.720
and destructive and I I I do believe
that but in terms of kind of where my

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.229
sympathy lies I have to go dig into this
without judgment and just try to

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:47.610
understand right I look at behavior and
I'm really just trying to understand

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:56.159
behavior not judge the behavior so I I
find Bobby Fischer fascinating and I

00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:07.680
have might kind of I guess assessments
as as I apply them to how I'm portraying

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.329
him.
Film Courage: Did playing Bobby Fischer give you any

00:02:12.329 --> 00:02:20.579
epiphanies about your own life? Tobey: I feel
like I'm always learning. I don't I can't

00:02:20.579 --> 00:02:28.939
say epiphany like as in there was some
you know big moment that I I took away

00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:36.719
some piece of knowledge or insight that
I had never had before or that made me

00:02:36.719 --> 00:02:43.019
like take a radical shift in my life but
but I I certainly learned things through

00:02:43.019 --> 00:02:45.620
the process.

